## [upstream] dht: read the J matrix sequentially in gsl_dht_apply

Commit: cd29899de

`gsl_dht_apply()` addressed the lower-triangular `Jjj` matrix with per-element
index arithmetic.  The entries are now stored in the order in which they are
consumed (`t->Jjj[m*size + i]`), built once in `gsl_dht_init()`, so the
transform reads them sequentially.  The result is unchanged; `Jjj` grows from
`size*(size+1)/2` to `size*size` doubles.  The original patch's error path
returned `GSL_SUCCESS` on allocation failure and freed the handle; this
version returns `GSL_ENOMEM` and leaves the handle to the caller.

File: `dht/dht.c`.

Based on the patch posted to help-gsl by Felipe Attanasio,
<https://www.mail-archive.com/help-gsl@gnu.org/msg05473.html>.


## [upstream] specfunc: compute the 3j symbol by edge recursion

Commit: 1b2c8ff98

`gsl_sf_coupling_3j_e()` evaluated the Racah formula directly with an
alternating sum, which loses precision for large angular momenta.  It now
uses the edge-recursion algorithm of Tuzun, Diz and Olcay-Cakir (1998), as
implemented by A. A. Illarionov, removing the cancellation.  6j and 9j
symbols are expressed in terms of 3j and follow automatically.  The 720-entry
argument-permutation table is in the new file `specfunc/coupling3j_regge.c`,
added to both build systems.

Files: `specfunc/coupling.c`, `specfunc/coupling3j_regge.c`,
`specfunc/Makefile.am`, `cmake/gsl_sources.cmake`.

Based on `coupling3j.patch` from Savannah bug #39473.


## [upstream] multimin: add a quadratic minimiser

Commit: 53cd0d098

New `gsl_multimin_fminimizer_quadratic`, a derivative-free minimiser for
nearly quadratic functions.  It minimises along each coordinate in turn by
fitting a parabola through the current point and the two points one step
away, moving to the predicted minimum when it improves the value and halving
the step otherwise.  The parabolic step is exact for a quadratic, so it
converges in a few sweeps; it can be slow when the coordinates are strongly
correlated.

Files: `multimin/quadratic.c`, `multimin/gsl_multimin.h`,
`multimin/Makefile.am`, `multimin/test.c`, `doc/multimin.rst`,
`cmake/gsl_sources.cmake`.

Based on the routine suggested by Jussi Lehtola in Savannah bug #32776.


